<title>FRANCE: Juppe laments &quot;bad&quot; French job figures.</title>
<headline>Juppe laments &quot;bad&quot; French job figures.</headline>
<dateline>LE HAVRE, France 1996-09-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister Alain Juppe said on Friday the surge in unemployment in August was bad news and acknowledged that the figures would not help to end criticism from within the ranks of his centre-right coalition.</p>
<p>&quot;The unemployment figures for the month of August are bad,&quot; Juppe said.</p>
<p>&quot;The bad unemployment figures published this morning will undoubtedly not help put an end to criticism within the ranks of the majority,&quot; Juppe told fellow deputies from his Gaullist RPR party at an annual conference.</p>
</text>
